-- of_bytes and drain --
a whole value round-trips: 5 bytes, hello
an empty source drains to nothing: 0 bytes, 
chunks are joined in order: 7 bytes, abcdefg
-- limited --
under the ceiling: 7 bytes, abcdefg
over it: the stream is too large: more than 5 bytes
drain's own ceiling says the same: the stream is too large: more than 5 bytes
a ceiling of zero admits nothing: the stream is too large: more than 0 bytes
-- an error is terminal --
a failed chunk ends the stream: the stream closed: the peer hung up
and mapped converts another error into this one: the stream failed: read error 5
-- text across chunk boundaries --
one byte at a time: [a][ö][b][→][c]
two bytes at a time: [a][öb][→c]
all at once: [aöb→c]
truncated: [a]<the stream is malformed: the stream ends in the middle of a UTF-8 character>
not UTF-8 at all: <the stream is malformed: the stream is not UTF-8>
-- lines --
mixed endings: [one][two][three]
one byte at a time: [one][two][three]
just a newline: []
empty: 
a split character in a line: [aö][b→]
